WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:01.770
The opening temple-raid sequence

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.140
of "Raiders of the Lost Ark"

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:05.770
is one of the best movie
openings of all time

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:07.560
because it reveals
everything you need to know

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.200
about Indiana Jones,
all in only 10 minutes.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.140
It shows that he is clever
and goes with his gut feeling.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.770
Indy makes plenty of mistakes,

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:22.030
but he always keeps trying,
even in the face of defeat.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:25.020
His determination and his
tendency to make mistakes

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.090
are Indy's two defining characteristics

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.420
throughout the franchise.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.040
And the film introduces the
audience to these qualities

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.870
right from the start.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:34.190
Now, compare that to the intro

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:36.000
from "Lara Croft: Tomb Raider,"

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.910
a movie that borrowed
heavily from "Indiana Jones."

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:41.760
Chances are you forgot
how this movie starts.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.850
To refresh your memory,
Lara fights a giant robot.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.660
She's acrobatic and
skilled at using pistols,

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.780
but that's about the only
thing we learn about her

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.500
in the first five minutes.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:53.420
Or take "The Mummy," where, again,

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.220
essentially the only thing we
learn about the protagonist

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:59.960
in his first scene is that
he's good at shooting guns.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:02.800
So, what exactly is the
intro to "Indiana Jones"

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.350
doing differently from its imitators?

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:08.870
While the acting, directing,
and editing are all superb,

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.350
what really sets this
opening sequence apart

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:12.670
from most other films

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:16.430
is that it's a self-contained
story that's well structured.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:17.850
We meet Indiana Jones

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:20.410
and watch him struggle
through multiple obstacles

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:21.950
to try and reach his goal.

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:24.260
In fact, this opening sequence

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:26.110
has a similar narrative arrangement

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:28.080
to that of a feature-length film

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.510
and actually fits
perfectly into the format

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:32.700
of a traditional three-act structure,

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.350
a screenplay structure
popularized by author Syd Field.

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:39.000
The three-act structure
expands upon the concept

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.340
of beginning, middle, and end.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.990
Let's take a look at the entirety
of "Star Wars: A New Hope"

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:45.190
as an example.

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:47.700
In act one, there's the beginning:

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.460
setting up the story.

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:50.770
The inciting incident:

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:53.250
an event that sets the story into motion.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:54.900
The climax of act one:

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:57.350
an event that signals that
the protagonist's life

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.100
will never be the same again.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:02.080
In act two there's rising action:

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.690
The protagonist is met
with new challenges.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:05.740
The midpoint:

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:07.560
Something goes terribly wrong,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.960
altering the plans of the protagonist.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.720
The climax of act two:

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:14.010
The protagonist hits their lowest point.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:16.520
In act three there's the climax:

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:17.800
the most intense point,

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:19.860
where the story's overarching conflict

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.050
is on the brink of being resolved.

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:23.890
And finally, the resolution:

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:26.910
wrapping up the story and
leading towards closure.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:28.370
Now, most movies,

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:30.520
including "Star Wars" and "Indiana Jones,"

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:31.920
tell their three-act stories

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.610
over the course of their
90-plus-minute run times.

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:35.920
What makes the opening sequence

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.140
of "Raiders of the Lost Ark" so special

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:41.700
is that it also creates a
mini three-act-structure story

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.340
in only 10 minutes.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:46.670
The camera follows a mysterious
character and his porters

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:49.030
making their way through a jungle.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:51.970
One of the porters pulls a gun
on the mysterious character,

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:54.330
but the man uses a whip to disarm him.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:58.040
We're officially introduced
to Indiana Jones.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:02:59.510
After entering the temple,

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:01.700
Indy intentionally activates a trap,

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:04.283
which reveals the skeleton
of his former rival.

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:08.090
Indiana and Satipo forge
deeper into the cave,

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:10.770
navigating their way past more traps.

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:13.470
Indiana Jones retrieves the golden idol

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:15.350
but accidentally triggers a trap,

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:17.780
and the temple starts
to collapse behind him.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.500
Indy is betrayed by Satipo,

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:22.240
and the temple doors start to close.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:24.310
Just when Indy thinks
that he's in the clear,

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:27.080
a giant boulder starts
to hurdle towards him.

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:29.990
Indy is alive, but he has to
hand over the idol and his gun

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:31.960
to another one of his rivals.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:34.250
By writing the opening of
"Raiders of the Lost Ark"

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:35.380
as a mini-movie,

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:37.730
it serves as a teaser
for the rest of the film

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:39.410
and allows the audience to get to know

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.980
what kind of world
they're about to explore.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:43.370
Compare that to the structure

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:45.080
of the opening of "Tomb Raider,"

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:48.740
which only has a beginning and
a climax, nothing in between.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:51.870
Her obstacle stays the
same the entire time,

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.100
the killer robot,

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:56.180
and she never really changes
her approach to defeating it,

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:57.880
shooting it with her guns.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:00.080
On the other hand, the
temple raid presents Indy

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.030
with a plethora of obstacles,

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:04.140
and we get to watch as he
comes up with solutions

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.050
for each new problem.

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:08.700
While the film itself has
some problematic moments,

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:10.920
from a purely filmmaking perspective,

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:13.200
the excellent structuring
of the opening sequence

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.450
of "Raiders of the Lost Ark"

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:17.710
makes it an unforgettable
introduction to Indiana Jones.

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:18.710
And at the end of it,

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:20.840
the audience feels like
they know the character

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:22.848
and the world that he inhabits.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:26.470
Thanks for watching.

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:28.740
Make sure to subscribe and
let us know in the comments

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.790
which movies you'd like us to cover next.

